{
  "title": "Counting and totals",
  "summary": "COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN and MAX squash many rows into one answer.",
  "minutes": 11,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Avalon Spokes",
      "body": [
        "Week two. Rosa sends you across town to **Avalon Spokes**, the city bike-share. Their operations lead, Teodor, has a spreadsheet habit and a question a minute: *how many rides? how long? how much money?*",
        "",
        "Those are **aggregate** questions: many rows in, one answer out.",
        "",
        "```sql",
        "SELECT COUNT(*)      AS rides,",
        "       SUM(fare)     AS revenue,",
        "       AVG(minutes)  AS avg_minutes,",
        "       MIN(minutes)  AS shortest,",
        "       MAX(minutes)  AS longest",
        "FROM rides;",
        "```",
        "",
        "That returns **one row**, however many rides there are."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this return?",
      "code": "SELECT COUNT(*), MIN(minutes), MAX(minutes) FROM rides;",
      "setup": [
        "CREATE TABLE rides (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, bike TEXT, rider_id INTEGER, start_station TEXT, end_station TEXT, started TEXT, minutes INTEGER, fare REAL, plan TEXT, rating INTEGER);",
        "INSERT INTO rides VALUES (1,'B07',101,'Harbour Gate','Lantern Square','2026-06-01 08:05',12,2.0,'member',5),(2,'B12',102,'Lantern Square','Mill Bridge','2026-06-01 08:20',7,1.5,'member',4),(3,'B03',103,'University Row','Fennel Park','2026-06-01 09:10',25,4.5,'casual',NULL),(4,'B07',104,'Lantern Square','Harbour Gate','2026-06-01 12:40',15,3.0,'casual',3),(5,'B21',101,'Lantern Square','Harbour Gate','2026-06-01 17:45',13,2.0,'member',5),(6,'B12',105,'Mill Bridge','Kestrel Point','2026-06-01 18:30',31,5.5,'casual',2),(7,'B03',106,'Fennel Park','University Row','2026-06-02 07:55',22,2.5,'member',NULL),(8,'B15',102,'Mill Bridge','Lantern Square','2026-06-02 08:15',8,1.5,'member',5),(9,'B07',107,'Harbour Gate','Kestrel Point','2026-06-02 10:00',18,3.5,'casual',4),(10,'B21',103,'Kestrel Point','Harbour Gate','2026-06-02 11:30',16,3.0,'casual',NULL),(11,'B15',108,'University Row','Lantern Square','2026-06-02 13:05',40,6.5,'casual',1),(12,'B12',101,'Harbour Gate','Lantern Square','2026-06-02 17:50',12,2.0,'member',4),(13,'B03',104,'Lantern Square','University Row','2026-06-03 09:00',35,6.0,'casual',3),(14,'B07',106,'University Row','Fennel Park','2026-06-03 09:40',20,2.5,'member',5),(15,'B21',105,'Kestrel Point','Mill Bridge','2026-06-03 14:20',28,5.0,'casual',NULL),(16,'B15',102,'Lantern Square','Mill Bridge','2026-06-03 18:05',9,1.5,'member',4),(17,'B12',107,'Mill Bridge','Harbour Gate','2026-06-03 19:30',14,3.0,'casual',2),(18,'B03',108,'Fennel Park','Fennel Park','2026-06-03 23:10',3,1.0,'casual',NULL);"
      ],
      "answer": "18 | 3 | 40",
      "explain": "18 rides; the shortest was 3 minutes and the longest 40."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Monday's numbers",
      "prompt": [
        "Teodor wants three numbers for **2026-06-01**: the number of rides (**rides**), total **revenue** (sum of fare), and the **longest** ride in minutes.",
        "",
        "Rides that day have `started` beginning with `2026-06-01`.",
        "",
        "Table: `rides(id, bike, rider_id, start_station, end_station, started, minutes, fare, plan, rating)`. `rating` (1 to 5) is NULL when the rider skipped the survey; `plan` is `'member'` or `'casual'`."
      ],
      "starter": "-- Write your query below\n",
      "solution": [
        "SELECT COUNT(*) AS rides, SUM(fare) AS revenue, MAX(minutes) AS longest",
        "FROM rides",
        "WHERE started LIKE '2026-06-01%';"
      ],
      "setup": [
        "CREATE TABLE rides (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, bike TEXT, rider_id INTEGER, start_station TEXT, end_station TEXT, started TEXT, minutes INTEGER, fare REAL, plan TEXT, rating INTEGER);",
        "INSERT INTO rides VALUES (1,'B07',101,'Harbour Gate','Lantern Square','2026-06-01 08:05',12,2.0,'member',5),(2,'B12',102,'Lantern Square','Mill Bridge','2026-06-01 08:20',7,1.5,'member',4),(3,'B03',103,'University Row','Fennel Park','2026-06-01 09:10',25,4.5,'casual',NULL),(4,'B07',104,'Lantern Square','Harbour Gate','2026-06-01 12:40',15,3.0,'casual',3),(5,'B21',101,'Lantern Square','Harbour Gate','2026-06-01 17:45',13,2.0,'member',5),(6,'B12',105,'Mill Bridge','Kestrel Point','2026-06-01 18:30',31,5.5,'casual',2),(7,'B03',106,'Fennel Park','University Row','2026-06-02 07:55',22,2.5,'member',NULL),(8,'B15',102,'Mill Bridge','Lantern Square','2026-06-02 08:15',8,1.5,'member',5),(9,'B07',107,'Harbour Gate','Kestrel Point','2026-06-02 10:00',18,3.5,'casual',4),(10,'B21',103,'Kestrel Point','Harbour Gate','2026-06-02 11:30',16,3.0,'casual',NULL),(11,'B15',108,'University Row','Lantern Square','2026-06-02 13:05',40,6.5,'casual',1),(12,'B12',101,'Harbour Gate','Lantern Square','2026-06-02 17:50',12,2.0,'member',4),(13,'B03',104,'Lantern Square','University Row','2026-06-03 09:00',35,6.0,'casual',3),(14,'B07',106,'University Row','Fennel Park','2026-06-03 09:40',20,2.5,'member',5),(15,'B21',105,'Kestrel Point','Mill Bridge','2026-06-03 14:20',28,5.0,'casual',NULL),(16,'B15',102,'Lantern Square','Mill Bridge','2026-06-03 18:05',9,1.5,'member',4),(17,'B12',107,'Mill Bridge','Harbour Gate','2026-06-03 19:30',14,3.0,'casual',2),(18,'B03',108,'Fennel Park','Fennel Park','2026-06-03 23:10',3,1.0,'casual',NULL);"
      ],
      "check": "rows",
      "hints": [
        "Filter with `WHERE started LIKE '2026-06-01%'`.",
        "WHERE runs *before* the aggregates, so they only see that day's rows."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "COUNT(*) vs COUNT(column)",
      "body": [
        "Aggregates **skip NULLs**. That makes the different `COUNT`s mean different things:",
        "",
        "```sql",
        "COUNT(*)              -- rows",
        "COUNT(rating)         -- rows where rating is not NULL",
        "COUNT(DISTINCT bike)  -- different non-NULL bikes",
        "AVG(rating)           -- average of the ratings that exist (NULLs ignored, not treated as 0)",
        "```",
        "",
        "If you *want* missing ratings treated as zero, say so: `AVG(COALESCE(rating, 0))`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this return?",
      "code": "SELECT COUNT(*), COUNT(rating), COUNT(DISTINCT bike) FROM rides;",
      "setup": [
        "CREATE TABLE rides (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, bike TEXT, rider_id INTEGER, start_station TEXT, end_station TEXT, started TEXT, minutes INTEGER, fare REAL, plan TEXT, rating INTEGER);",
        "INSERT INTO rides VALUES (1,'B07',101,'Harbour Gate','Lantern Square','2026-06-01 08:05',12,2.0,'member',5),(2,'B12',102,'Lantern Square','Mill Bridge','2026-06-01 08:20',7,1.5,'member',4),(3,'B03',103,'University Row','Fennel Park','2026-06-01 09:10',25,4.5,'casual',NULL),(4,'B07',104,'Lantern Square','Harbour Gate','2026-06-01 12:40',15,3.0,'casual',3),(5,'B21',101,'Lantern Square','Harbour Gate','2026-06-01 17:45',13,2.0,'member',5),(6,'B12',105,'Mill Bridge','Kestrel Point','2026-06-01 18:30',31,5.5,'casual',2),(7,'B03',106,'Fennel Park','University Row','2026-06-02 07:55',22,2.5,'member',NULL),(8,'B15',102,'Mill Bridge','Lantern Square','2026-06-02 08:15',8,1.5,'member',5),(9,'B07',107,'Harbour Gate','Kestrel Point','2026-06-02 10:00',18,3.5,'casual',4),(10,'B21',103,'Kestrel Point','Harbour Gate','2026-06-02 11:30',16,3.0,'casual',NULL),(11,'B15',108,'University Row','Lantern Square','2026-06-02 13:05',40,6.5,'casual',1),(12,'B12',101,'Harbour Gate','Lantern Square','2026-06-02 17:50',12,2.0,'member',4),(13,'B03',104,'Lantern Square','University Row','2026-06-03 09:00',35,6.0,'casual',3),(14,'B07',106,'University Row','Fennel Park','2026-06-03 09:40',20,2.5,'member',5),(15,'B21',105,'Kestrel Point','Mill Bridge','2026-06-03 14:20',28,5.0,'casual',NULL),(16,'B15',102,'Lantern Square','Mill Bridge','2026-06-03 18:05',9,1.5,'member',4),(17,'B12',107,'Mill Bridge','Harbour Gate','2026-06-03 19:30',14,3.0,'casual',2),(18,'B03',108,'Fennel Park','Fennel Park','2026-06-03 23:10',3,1.0,'casual',NULL);"
      ],
      "answer": "18 | 13 | 5",
      "explain": "18 rows, 13 of them have a rating, and five different bikes did all the work."
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Three rides have ratings 4, 2 and NULL. What is `AVG(rating)`?",
      "options": [
        "3",
        "2",
        "NULL",
        "An error"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "shuffle": false,
      "explain": "The NULL is ignored, so it is (4 + 2) / 2 = 3. `AVG(COALESCE(rating, 0))` would give 2."
